  "fixture_sha256": "86dc74c167067a0ba97d47d309edbb48c4c22bbb5edf86b36dd6f7c05455b0ad",
  "depths_description": "Dimensionless binned transit depths from the independent per-species FP32 JAX diagnostic, including spot contamination and stellar-flux bin weighting. Each species is interpolated in log cross section on inverse-temperature and log-pressure axes before summing layer opacities. The unused combined-grid opacity diagnostic is omitted because it uses a different interpolation order. The legacy stellar spectra are independently evaluated with pymsg.SpecGrid.flux(order=1) on geometric edges around the R~1000 low-resolution wavelength centers, trimmed to the MSG domain and converted to SI F_lambda by multiplying by 1e7. At logg 5.5 and [Fe/H] +0.5, the isolated missing 2500 K row is repaired by averaging 2400 K and 2600 K before interpolation to 2550 K. Stellar rows are wavelength-interpolated to the 82 retained opacity samples and stored as FP32. The unchanged v6.3.1 per_species diagnostic independently computes the profile and binned depths; the reconstructed method reproduced the previous reference within 0.03 ppm before regeneration.",
  "parameters_description": "Generic round numerical benchmark inputs for reproducibility; the fixture contains model opacities and calculated spectra."
